<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
  <meta charset="UTF-8">
  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
  <title>XSS Labs - EliteHackLab</title>
  <link rel="stylesheet" href="/css/style.css">
  <link rel="stylesheet" href="https://cdnjs.cloudflare.com/ajax/libs/font-awesome/6.5.1/css/all.min.css">
</head>
<body>
  <div class="matrix-bg"></div>
  <nav class="main-nav">
    <div class="nav-brand"><span class="brand-icon">💀</span><span class="brand-text">Elite<span class="highlight">Hack</span>Lab</span></div>
    <div class="nav-links"><a href="/"><i class="fas fa-home"></i> Dashboard</a><a href="/scoreboard"><i class="fas fa-trophy"></i> Scoreboard</a></div>
  </nav>
  <div class="lab-container">
    <div class="lab-header">
      <div class="breadcrumb"><a href="/">Home</a> / XSS Labs</div>
      <h1>🎭 Cross-Site Scripting (XSS) Labs</h1>
    </div>
    <div class="lab-section">
      <h2><i class="fas fa-book"></i> Theory</h2>
      <p>XSS allows attackers to inject client-side scripts into web pages viewed by others. This can steal cookies, redirect users, deface websites, or perform actions on behalf of the victim.</p>
      <div class="code-block">
Types of XSS:
1. Reflected - Input reflected back in response (URL parameters)
2. Stored - Payload saved in database, affects all who view it
3. DOM-Based - Client-side JavaScript processes malicious input
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="lab-section">
      <h2><i class="fas fa-flask"></i> Available Labs</h2>
      <div class="lab-list">
        <% labs.forEach(function(lab) { %>
          <a href="<%= lab.path %>" class="lab-link">
            <span class="lab-name"><i class="fas fa-terminal"></i> <%= lab.name %></span>
            <span class="lab-difficulty <%= lab.difficulty.toLowerCase() %>"><%= lab.difficulty %></span>
          </a>
        <% }); %>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
  <script src="/js/main.js"></script>
</body>
</html>
